WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.550
A Chinese classic opens with a puzzle:
The Tao that can be trodden is not the

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:08.290
enduring and unchanging Tao.

3
00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:11.910
Tao means the Way, the
source of everything.

4
00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:15.170
Yet no fixed path or name can hold it.

5
00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:19.780
Taoist texts praise the newborn
child and the uncarved block:

6
00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.770
simple and natural.

7
00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:26.640
So why would a religion teach that the
best way to act is often to stop forcing

8
00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:27.840
things?

9
00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:30.920
In this mission, you'll
see how, in Taoist eyes,

10
00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:33.770
people drift out of tune with the Way.

11
00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:39.550
Then you'll explore yin and yang, and why
some Taoists seek to become immortals.

12
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:44.730
Your mission: find out why Taoists might
say the best action is often to stop

13
00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:45.950
forcing things.
